The '''Partido Nacional''' was a nationalist political party in Sarta that emerged after the [[Second War of the Isthmus]]. It was formed by [[Jaime Checa]], a volunteer fighter who returned from the war aligned with Volisanian fascist elements.

The party grew out of the backlash against the [[Union del Personajes]] and the anti-[[Volisania]] parliamentary majority that had been reluctant to support Volisania during the war. Its organisers argued that Sarta had been weakened by hesitation, labour unrest, and sympathy for foreign rivals, and they presented the party as a force for order and national revival.

== Formation ==

The party developed in the years after 1899, as the defeat of Volisania in the isthmus war became a domestic political issue. Jaime Checa and his allies built support among veterans, conservative voters, and figures who feared socialist agitation, and they aligned with the [[National Volisan Party|National Volisan Party (partit nacional volisà)]].

== Political position ==

The Partido Nacional combined nationalism, anti-socialism, and hostility to organised labour. It also used the wartime experience to argue that Sarta should align more closely with Volisanian fascist politics and reject the older anti-war parliamentary compromise.

== Electoral rise ==

The party took advantage of continuing strikes and protests in the 1890s and early 1900s, as well as the fear generated by the Darasian Socialist Revolution of 1904–1905. By 1906, it had won a majority of seats in the lower house.

